<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #0f1117;
    --card: #1a1d27;
    --card-hover: #22263a;
    --accent: #4f8cff;
    --accent2: #ff6b6b;
    --accent3: #ffd93d;
    --accent4: #6bcb77;
    --text: #e0e0e0;
    --text-muted: #8a8fa8;
    --border: #2a2e3f;
    --red: #ff4757;
    --orange: #ffa502;
    --green: #2ed573;
    --iran: #8e44ad;
  }
  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; background: var(--bg); color: var(--text); line-height: 1.65; }
  .container { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }

  .hero { text-align: center; padding: 56px 20px 36px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a1d27 0%, #0f1117 100%); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .hero h1 { font-size: 2.2em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--accent), var(--accent2)); -webkit-background-clip: text; -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent; }
  .hero .subtitle { font-size: 1em; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto 16px; }
  .hero .date-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--accent); }
  .hero .war-day { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent2); color: #fff; border-radius: 20px; padding: 6px 18px; font-size: 0.85em; font-weight: 600; margin-left: 8px; }
  .hero .build-meta { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .triplet-badge { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #0e1a1e); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 8px; padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 0.75em; color: var(--accent); display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; }

  .direction-of-travel { max-width: 900px; margin: 24px auto; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2235, #1a1d27); border: 2px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 28px; font-size: 1.05em; line-height: 1.55; }
  .direction-of-travel .label { font-size: 0.72em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .direction-of-travel .body { color: var(--text); }
  .direction-of-travel .body .cite { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move { border-color: var(--border); }
  .direction-of-travel.no-move .body { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }

  .disclaimer { background: #2a1a1a; border: 1px solid #5a2020; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 20px; margin: 24px auto; max-width: 900px; font-size: 0.85em; color: #ffaaaa; }
  .disclaimer strong { color: var(--accent2); }

  .section { padding: 30px 0; }
  .section-title { font-size: 1.5em; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; }
  .section-title .meta { font-size: 0.6em; color: var(--text-muted); font-weight: 400; }

  /* === FORECAST BOARD === */
  .forecast-board { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label { font-size: 0.75em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 14px 0 4px; padding-left: 4px; }
  .forecast-bucket-label:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .forecast-card { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 20px; }
  .forecast-card.cat-diplomacy { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card.cat-military { border-left-color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card.cat-regime { border-left-color: var(--iran); }
  .forecast-card.cat-market { border-left-color: var(--accent3); }
  .forecast-card.cat-domestic { border-left-color: var(--accent4); }
  .forecast-card.cat-humanitarian { border-left-color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-id { font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.7em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-category { font-size: 0.7em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--text-muted); padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-question { font-size: 1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; line-height: 1.45; }
  .forecast-card .fc-probrow { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px; margin-bottom: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.8em; font-weight: 800; color: var(--accent); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta { font-size: 0.9em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-up { color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.move-down { color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta.no-move { color: var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-horizon { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-delta-reason { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin: 6px 0 10px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; margin-top: 8px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card .fc-meta-row dd { color: var(--text); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicators { font-size: 0.82em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 6px; }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; margin: 2px; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-OBSERVED { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); border-color: var(--green); color: var(--green); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-PARTIAL { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); border-color: var(--orange); color: var(--orange); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-CONTRADICTED { background: rgba(255, 71, 87, 0.15); border-color: var(--red); color: var(--red); }
  .forecast-card .fc-indicator.state-NOT_OBSERVED { color: var(--text-muted); }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE { opacity: 0.55; border-left-style: dashed; }
  .forecast-card.status-OBE .fc-question::after { content: ' [OBE]'; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .forecast-empty-slot { background: transparent; border: 1px dashed var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === DELTA SECTION === */
  .delta-narrative p { color: var(--text); font-size: 0.96em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .delta-narrative p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.88em; }
  .delta-narrative p .context-only { color: var(--text-muted); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* === SCENARIO MAP === */
  .scenario-map { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .prob-bar-container { display: flex; height: 36px; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .prob-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85em; color: #fff; }
  .prob-escalation { background: var(--red); }
  .prob-status { background: var(--orange); }
  .prob-deescalation { background: var(--green); }
  .scenario-line { font-size: 0.92em; color: var(--text); margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .scenario-line strong.label-esc { color: var(--red); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-prot { color: var(--orange); }
  .scenario-line strong.label-desc { color: var(--green); }

  /* === INSIDE IRAN === */
  .inside-iran { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .inside-iran p { font-size: 0.93em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .inside-iran p .cite { color: var(--accent); font-family: 'SF Mono', Menlo, monospace; font-size: 0.85em; }
  .iran-media-badges { display: flex; gap: 6px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .iran-media-badge { display: inline-block; padding: 2px 8px; border: 1px solid var(--iran); border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.72em; color: var(--iran); }

  /* === REGIME CHANGE WATCH === */
  .regime-watch { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 22px; }
  .regime-watch-meta { font-size: 0.8em; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .regime-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; padding: 10px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .regime-row:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  .regime-row .name { font-weight: 600; }
  .regime-row .p { font-size: 1.4em; font-weight: 700; color: var(--orange); }
  .regime-row .drivers { font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--text-muted); flex-basis: 100%; margin-top: 4px; }

  /* === SOURCES === */
  .sources-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  .sources-list li { padding: 8px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 0.88em; display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sources-list a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .sources-list a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .source-tier { display: inline-block; padding: 1px 8px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.7em; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.5px; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .source-tier.tier-TIER1 { background: rgba(46, 213, 115, 0.15); color: var(--green); border: 1px solid var(--green); }
  .source-tier.tier-OSINT { background: rgba(79, 140, 255, 0.15); color: var(--accent); border: 1px solid var(--accent); }
  .source-tier.tier-STATE_MEDIA { background: rgba(255, 165, 2, 0.15); color: var(--orange); border: 1px solid var(--orange); }
  .source-tier.tier-EXPERT { background: rgba(155, 89, 182, 0.15); color: #9b59b6; border: 1px solid #9b59b6; }

  /* === EXPERT APPENDIX === */
  .expert-appendix { background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; margin-top: 18px; }
  .expert-appendix summary { padding: 14px 20px; cursor: pointer; font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.92em; user-select: none; }
  .expert-appendix summary:hover { color: var(--text); }
  .expert-appendix[open] summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 20px 18px; }
  .expert-quote { padding: 10px 14px; border-left: 3px solid #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 12px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .expert-quote .expert-name { font-weight: 700; color: #9b59b6; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .expert-empty { color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic; font-size: 0.88em; }

  /* === FOOTER === */
  footer { text-align: center; padding: 32px 20px; color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8em; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin-top: 32px; }
  footer .next-update { color: var(--accent); }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .hero { padding: 36px 16px 24px; }
    .hero h1 { font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.3; }
    .container { padding: 12px; }
    .direction-of-travel { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 16px 18px; font-size: 0.95em; }
    .disclaimer { margin: 16px 12px; padding: 12px; font-size: 0.8em; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.2em; }
    .forecast-card { padding: 14px 16px; }
    .forecast-card .fc-p { font-size: 1.5em; }
    .scenario-map, .inside-iran, .regime-watch, .expert-appendix .expert-body { padding: 14px 16px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="hero">
  <h1>Geopolitical Scenario Analysis — Middle East</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Forecast board + descriptive delta. Predictions are time-bounded and scored; descriptions are sourced and verb-disciplined.</p>
  <span class="date-badge">August 20, 2026</span>
  <span class="war-day">Day 174 of the 2026 Iran War</span>
  <div class="build-meta">Published: <span id="pub-ts">2026-08-20T07:00:00Z</span> · Build <span id="build-id" style="font-family:monospace;opacity:0.6;">v49.0</span></div>
  <div class="triplet-badge">⚖ Triple-blind: Analyst + Devil's Advocate + Judge · forecast-board v45</div>
</div>

<div class="container">

  <!-- ========== 1. DIRECTION OF TRAVEL (written LAST by Judge) ========== -->
  <div class="direction-of-travel">
    <div class="label">Where this is heading</div>
    <div class="body">
      The Islamabad MOU ceasefire framework expired August 17 without renewal — <span class="cite">N5</span> RESOLVED-NO — and CENTCOM confirmed strikes on IRGC targets following Iran's August 18 ballistic missile attack on UAE; <span class="cite">N7</span>'s near-term strike probability at 22% and <span class="cite">N8</span>'s 21-day Iranian missile re-launch probability at 45% confirm the trajectory is active escalation, not managed pause.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="disclaimer">
    <strong>⚠ DISCLAIMER:</strong> This analysis relies on open sources (OSINT) and AI-generated assessments. Probabilities are time-bounded forecasts with resolution criteria; track record visible internally until ≥20 forecasts resolve. Descriptive sections enforce verb discipline — any causal/directional claim must cite a forecast or be marked context-only.
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 2. FORECAST BOARD ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="forecast-board">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Forecast Board
      <span class="meta">7 active · last reasoned 2026-08-20</span>
    </h2>

    <div class="forecast-board">

      <!-- NEAR-TERM (≤72h) -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">Near-Term (≤72h)</div>

      <!-- N7: CENTCOM strikes inside Iran by Aug 23 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N7 · 2026-08-20-us-strike-iran-territory-by-aug-23</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will CENTCOM confirm airstrikes specifically targeting locations inside Iranian territorial borders before EOD 2026-08-23?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">22%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (no prior)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-08-23</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Ceasefire terminated Aug 19; CENTCOM conducted strikes on IRGC targets in response to Iran UAE missiles (Art. 4559495). Pattern of resumed strikes now established. DA audit correctly notes Trump's rhetoric-vs-action gap warrants discount from 0.30 base to 0.22 (19-night pause pattern shows both sides retain capacity for restraint; UAE missile strike response may have been limited strike on non-Iranian-territory IRGC assets). 72-hour window is narrow; absence of carrier repositioning to attack posture (NOT_OBSERVED) also constrains upside.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM or US DoD official statement, or two independent TIER1 sources, confirm US airstrikes on targets physically located inside Iranian territory before EOD 2026-08-23. Strikes on IRGC proxies, IRGC assets outside Iran, or Iran-aligned forces in third countries = NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM official press release naming Iranian territory or provinces, plus one TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNN), OR two independent TIER1 sources.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>CENTCOM statement referencing 'Iranian-linked' or 'IRGC-affiliated' targets without confirming location inside Iran = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Naval or missile exchanges in Hormuz not targeting Iranian soil = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM statement naming Iranian provinces or territory as strike location</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Israeli or US satellite imagery of Iranian facility circulated by TIER1</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 7-30 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">7–30 Days</div>

      <!-- N2: Iran nuclear WG session by Sep 1 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N2 · 2026-08-17-iran-confirms-nuclear-wg-session-by-sep-01</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran publicly confirm participation in a new, formally-structured nuclear working-group session (direct or mediated) before EOD 2026-09-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">7%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta move-down">↓ −23pp from 30% (2026-08-17)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Trump stated Aug 18 'no talks underway or scheduled with Iran'; MOU framework expired Aug 19 without renewal; CENTCOM conducted strikes on IRGC targets Aug 19–20; Iranian MFA Araghchi stated Iran 'has not decided whether to resume negotiations.' Active military operations preclude a formal nuclear working-group session within the 12-day remaining window. No indicator observed.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if TIER1 reports Iran's MFA or named Iranian envoy publicly confirms attendance at/convening of a nuclear-specific working-group session (enrichment, stockpile, or verification) before EOD 2026-09-01.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Reuters/AP/AFP/Al Jazeera plus Iranian MFA confirmation OR mediator (Oman/Pakistan/Qatar) readout.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Indirect confirmation via mediator without Iranian MFA confirmation = AMBIGUOUS. Iranian statement of 'willingness' without dated session = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Iran MFA spokesman names date or venue for nuclear working-group session</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Omani or Pakistani mediator readout of upcoming nuclear session</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N8: Iran ballistic missiles GCC by Sep 10 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N8 · 2026-08-20-iran-ballistic-gcc-by-sep-10</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will Iran's armed forces launch ballistic missiles targeting GCC territory (Saudi Arabia, UAE, Qatar, Kuwait, Bahrain, Jordan) or a US military installation before EOD 2026-09-10?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">45%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (no prior)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-10</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Iran launched two ballistic missiles at UAE Aug 18 (confirmed UAE air defense + CNBC). Ceasefire terminated Aug 19; no deterrence structure in place. The Aug 18 UAE strike demonstrates IRGC willingness to use ballistic missiles against GCC states. Without a replacement framework, 21 days provides substantial window for recurrence. UAE trade suspension (Aug 19) removes economic channel that historically limited IRGC strikes on UAE assets.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if TIER1 and official government source confirm Iranian armed forces (IRGC/IRGC-ASF) launched ballistic missiles at GCC state territory or US military installation before EOD 2026-09-10. Cruise missiles count; drones alone do NOT count for this forecast.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNN/Al Jazeera) OR one TIER1 plus official government statement (UAE/Saudi/Qatar/US CENTCOM) confirming Iranian ballistic missile origin.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Proxy IRGC-affiliated forces (Houthis, Hezbollah, Kataib Hezbollah) without direct IRGC launch order confirmed by TIER1 = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Drones only (no ballistic component) = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">UAE or Saudi air defense activation with confirmed interception of Iranian ballistic missile</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM or TIER1 confirms IRGC launch order for ballistic missile against GCC state</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N9: US-Iran diplomatic contact by Sep 15 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-diplomacy status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N9 · 2026-08-20-us-iran-diplomatic-contact-by-sep-15</span>
          <span class="fc-category">diplomacy</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will a named US official and a named Iranian official hold confirmed direct or mediated contact in any format (face-to-face, phone, or written exchange via named mediator) before EOD 2026-09-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">30%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (no prior)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Despite Trump's Aug 18 denial of 'talks,' his earlier same-day claim of an IRGC back-channel (later walked back) and historical precedent of informal contact persisting through open hostilities (Oman track) provide a credible pathway. Named-officials contact — even via Omani intermediary letter relay — would satisfy resolution criteria. 26-day window is long enough for at least one informal mediated exchange. Probability constrained by the resumption of active strikes and Trump's public hardline stance.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if TIER1 confirms named US and Iranian officials exchanged direct or formally mediated communications before EOD 2026-09-15. Relay of written messages via named mediator (Oman, Qatar, Pakistan) counts if both US and Iranian sides are identified. General claims of 'back-channel' without named officials = NO.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Two TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/Axios/Bloomberg) OR one TIER1 plus official US/Iranian government confirmation of named contact.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Unnamed 'US officials' or unnamed 'Iranian sources' reporting back-channel = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Social media or public speech as substitute for direct contact = NO. One side confirming contact without the other = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Omani or Qatari mediator named as relay for US-Iran written exchange</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">Trump or Rubio confirms back-channel with named Iranian interlocutor</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- N11: Iran leadership targeting by Sep 15 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-military status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N11 · 2026-08-20-iran-leadership-targeting-by-sep-15</span>
          <span class="fc-category">military</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the US or Israel confirm or claim responsibility for a targeted strike against a named Iranian senior official (minister-level or above, IRGC major general or above, or Supreme Leader) before EOD 2026-09-15?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">18%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (no prior)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-09-15</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. With ceasefire terminated and CENTCOM conducting strikes on IRGC targets, the precedent of decapitation strikes — Fox News reporting CENTCOM commander directed strike against IRGC headquarters/underground facility — combined with 26-day window creates a non-trivial probability. However, Mojtaba Khamenei installed as Supreme Leader March 2026 with IRGC cohesion maintained per Aug 17 regime-watch assessment; decapitation would require a significant escalation decision above current CENTCOM posture. Probability balanced at 0.18 above base rate for a ceasefire period.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if CENTCOM, IDF, or official US/Israeli government statement, or two independent TIER1 sources, confirm a targeted strike aimed at a named Iranian official of minister-level or above, IRGC major general or above, or the Supreme Leader (Mojtaba Khamenei) before EOD 2026-09-15. Confirmed attempt = YES; does not require target was killed.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>CENTCOM or IDF official statement, OR two independent TIER1 (Reuters/AP/AFP/CNN/Al Jazeera) confirming targeted strike on named Iranian official.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Strike on unnamed IRGC figures or general air campaign without specific named-target indication = NO. Iranian state media attribution without corroborating TIER1 = AMBIGUOUS-RESOLVE-AS-NO. Below minister/major-general rank = NO.</dd>
        </dl>
        <div class="fc-indicators">
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">TIER1 reports targeted kill or strike on named Iranian senior official</span>
          <span class="fc-indicator state-NOT_OBSERVED">CENTCOM or IDF statement confirming leadership targeting operation in Iran</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 30-90 DAYS -->
      <div class="forecast-bucket-label">30–90 Days</div>

      <!-- N10: Hormuz ≥5/day by Oct 1 -->
      <div class="forecast-card cat-market status-ACTIVE">
        <div class="fc-head">
          <span class="fc-id">N10 · 2026-08-20-hormuz-5vessels-7day-by-oct-01</span>
          <span class="fc-category">market</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-question">Will the Strait of Hormuz commercial vessel transit rate reach a 7-day average of 5 or more vessels per day at any point before EOD 2026-10-01?</div>
        <div class="fc-probrow">
          <span class="fc-p">18%</span>
          <span class="fc-delta no-move">New forecast (no prior)</span>
          <span class="fc-horizon">→ resolves by 2026-10-01</span>
        </div>
        <div class="fc-delta-reason">New forecast. Current Hormuz transit: approximately 1 vessel/day as of Aug 16 (UKMTO data; ~1.4% of pre-conflict 73/day baseline). War-risk insurance at 40× pre-crisis; 6 P&I clubs withdrew cover; UAE cut trade links with Iran Aug 19; ceasefire terminated. Getting from 1/day to ≥5/day (7-day avg) within 42 days requires either a security framework or a unilateral insurer decision to accept elevated risk — both are low-probability given the escalation trajectory. Threshold set at 5/day (vs. N4's 30/day) to reflect the realistic lower bound of functional, albeit minimal, commercial navigation.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if IMF PortWatch or equivalent AIS tracker (Windward, TankerMap) records a 7-day trailing average of ≥5 commercial vessel transits/day through the Hormuz chokepoint at any point before EOD 2026-10-01. Naval warships do NOT count.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>IMF PortWatch or Windward/TankerMap data plus one TIER1 shipping source (Bloomberg/Reuters/Lloyd's List). If PortWatch unpublished, use Windward and flag AMBIGUOUS if trackers conflict by >50%.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>Naval escorts and warships do NOT count toward commercial threshold. One-off single-day spikes without a sustained 7-day average ≥5 = NO. Military-escorted commercial convoys count if the vessels themselves are commercial.</dd>
