  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA (descriptive, verb-disciplined) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>Iran's armed forces launched two ballistic missiles at UAE waters on August 18, with UAE air defense systems confirming interceptions near the Abu Dhabi-Dubai corridor (CNBC, Aug 19 2026). CENTCOM, in press release Art. 4559495, confirmed US forces conducted strikes on IRGC targets in response to the Iranian launch — the two events together constitute a direct US-Iran military exchange and the cessation of the ceasefire period. → moved <span class="cite">N1</span>, <span class="cite">N5</span></p>
      <p>The Islamabad MOU ceasefire framework expired on August 17 without renewal. President Trump, in a White House official communication on August 19, declared the arrangement formally 'no longer in effect' — a named official with declaratory authority, satisfying N5's ambiguity rule for non-tweet formal executive action. The UAE simultaneously announced a full suspension of trade links with Iran (Gulf News, Aug 19 2026), removing the economic channel that had previously constrained IRGC targeting calculus against Gulf states. → moved <span class="cite">N5</span></p>
      <p>With the MOU framework expired and CENTCOM-IRGC exchanges confirmed, Iran's MFA spokesman Araghchi stated August 18 that Iran 'has not decided whether to resume negotiations'; Trump confirmed the same day that 'no talks are underway or scheduled with Iran.' The combination of formal ceasefire termination and active military operations forecloses a nuclear working-group session within the 12-day remaining window for N2; the forecast moves from 0.30 to 0.07. → moved <span class="cite">N2</span></p>
      <p>On the Israeli political front, the August 9–12 Kan poll records Eisenkot's Yashar party at 23 Knesset seats against Likud's 21; a JPost poll from approximately August 15 corroborates a 2-mandate Yashar lead. Netanyahu's caretaker coalition held approximately 48 Knesset seats, below the 61-seat majority threshold. N6 moves from 0.45 to 0.32 on the Aug poll data; no Regime Change Watch update today (Thursday — weekly cadence, next review August 23). → moved <span class="cite">N6</span></p>
      <p>UKMTO data and Windward AIS records from August 16 place Hormuz commercial transits at approximately 1 vessel/day — roughly 1.4% of the pre-conflict 73/day baseline. War-risk insurance stands at approximately 40× pre-crisis rates; six P&I clubs have withdrawn Hormuz cover; ceasefire termination closed the sole framework for near-term recovery. The prior N4 forecast (≥30/day by Oct 1) was retired OBE as impractical at current transit levels; N10 opens at 0.18 (≥5/day by Oct 1) as the operative recovery tracking threshold. → moved <span class="cite">N10</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

