      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (40%):</strong> Active exchanges continue without either side crossing a threshold that forces a decisive engagement or a new ceasefire framework — N9 (named diplomatic contact by Sep 15, 30%) staying unresolved is the principal marker for this path.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> Requires both N7 and N8 to resolve NO and N9 to resolve YES — a combination that is low-probability given the expired MOU framework and the absence of any active mediator channel as of August 20.</p>
