  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media (IRNA, Tasnim, Fars) carried the August 18 ballistic missile launch against UAE waters as a 'proportionate deterrent response to foreign aggression,' with the IRGC Aerospace Force communiqué asserting the strikes targeted 'hostile military infrastructure' without specifying precise impact locations. The MOU expiry and ceasefire termination received no direct coverage in official state channels through August 20. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
      <p>IRNA on August 20 reproduced Araghchi's statement that Iran's 'position on nuclear diplomacy remains clear and unchanged,' declining to confirm or deny any back-channel contact with Washington. No IRNA or Tasnim report named the MOU as an expired framework or characterized August 19 US strikes as a resumption of full-scale hostilities — state media framed them as isolated 'retaliatory aggression' rather than systematic escalation. N2 (nuclear WG session by Sep 1, 7%) has no pathway that does not require an MFA about-face on this public framing. → supports <span class="cite">N2</span></p>
      <p>Kayhan and Tasnim both characterized CENTCOM operations against IRGC targets as 'illegal acts of aggression against the Islamic Republic' and called for 'firm and decisive response.' The Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei — installed March 2026 with IRGC cohesion maintained — made no public statement through August 20. Regime Change Watch inherits the August 17 range (Iran 10–20%) with no intra-week review today. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

